# `KEYWORD-RENAME-SCOPE` + core §1/`GENRE-NAMESPACE`: a multi-section file carries the VERSION and the GENRE per
# SECTION, so the connector gate is evaluated per section too. Section 1 is a
# `figdown 0.1 flowchart` and spells the line `edge`; section 2 is a
# `figdown 0.2 flowchart` in the SAME FILE and spells it `flowline`. Both are
# legal, and each section resolves against its own header — this is the case
# that proves the gate is not a per-file switch.
figdown 0.1 flowchart
title "Section 1 — 0.1 vocabulary"
process a "Step"
process b "Step 2"
edge a -> b

figdown 0.2 flowchart
title "Section 2 — 0.2 vocabulary"
process c "Step"
process d "Step 2"
flowline c -> d
